16:["$","$L2e",null,{"type":"multiple","children":[["$","$L2f",null,{"title":"Why does this run the worker in the same process as the CAS?","id":"why-does-this-run-the-worker-in-the-same-process-as-the-cas","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Because it's the fewest moving parts that still exercises the real code\npaths: the worker here uses the same gRPC worker API, the same scheduler,\nand the same store implementations a production cluster does. Splitting into\nseparate processes changes the deployment, not the protocol. See\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/production-config","children":"Production configuration"}]," for the split\nversion."]}]}],["$","$L2f",null,{"title":"Can I keep using this for day-to-day local builds?","id":"can-i-keep-using-this-for-day-to-day-local-builds","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["You can, and some people do; a single-process cluster is a reasonable way\nto get sandboxed, cached builds on one machine. But it gives you no\nparallelism beyond one worker's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"cpu_count"}],", and the filesystem stores are\npointed at ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/tmp"}],". ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/remote-execution/local-testing","children":"Local testing"}]," covers\nthe longer-lived version of this setup."]}]}],["$","$L2f",null,{"title":"What if I'm not using Bazel?","id":"what-if-im-not-using-bazel","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["The cluster is build-tool agnostic: it speaks the Remote Execution API, and\nBuck2, Siso, Pants, and recc all connect to the same endpoints.\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/getting-started/connect-your-build","children":"Connect your build"}]," has the flag\nequivalents. The verification step differs per tool; look for whatever your\ntool calls its execution strategy in its own logs."]}]}],["$","$L2f",null,{"title":"Where did my data go, and how do I clean it up?","id":"where-did-my-data-go-and-how-do-i-clean-it-up","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Everything this config writes lives under\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"/tmp/forge-local-rbe-test/"}],": CAS content, action cache, the worker's\nfast store, and its work directory. Stop the server and delete that tree to\nstart clean."]}]}]]}]
